# What is true about the host this runs on. Copy to deploy/host.env there;
# absent on a laptop, and every default below reproduces the unproxied
# behaviour exactly.

# The two hostnames, which must already resolve here. Setting both is what makes
# ./up.sh start Caddy and ask Let's Encrypt for certificates. A bare IP cannot
# have one, so leave these blank until DNS exists.
LIBVOX_PORTAL_DOMAIN=
LIBVOX_WIDGET_DOMAIN=

# Setting the second one is half the job. The other half lives in
# libvox-portal/.env, which is what the Assistant screen prints into the line a
# library pastes into its OPAC:
#
#   LIBVOX_WIDGET_URL=https://<the same widget domain>
#
# Nothing fails when those two disagree -- the stack comes up, every panel
# works, and the snippet loads nothing. `./up.sh` compares them and says so.

# The interface 8090 and 8092 bind to. Behind the proxy set 127.0.0.1: Caddy
# reaches the containers by name over libvox_internal, so leaving them on the
# network would offer the same panel over plain HTTP beside the one with TLS.
LIBVOX_BIND=0.0.0.0
